th the rock work but sometimes it's  just fun to let yourself go in this take  all kinds of scenery and see what you  can do with that and that's kind of what  I did in this case although I must be  very honest I wasn't really too creative  with the rock work over here yes that is  a penis right there I was streaming and  then that was actually not a penis  because I like immature shapes but  because I wanted to create a little  camera  a little spot where I would have an open  area in the forest from which I could  take pictures or videos or just in  general my shots so that's why the penis  is over there it's a functional penis  don't worry what was I talking about  though then I think I completely lost  the subject well that's um that's a  problem isn't it I won't wait wait are  we talking about yeah the problem that I  felt with this park almost was as  over-the-top as a rock workmate might  seem it's not that creative but then  again there is a problem and you might  want to write this down because there's  just a very limited list of rock sets  out there there is Weber's foliage set  which got mossy rocks and a couple of  other things and they're very nice but  they only really work for Massey  environments forests and stuff like that  sometimes people use them for  Riverside's I guess that works waivers  large rocks which is generally like the  name suggests a set with large box when  you expect there's Weber's medium rocks  which unlike the name suggests has  completely different textures than large  rocks so do be wary of that and there is  shy guys rock set which is somewhat  outdated but it's still got some users  there is Yosemite set by MGP which got  those amazing big rocks that you can  really use for some mountain sides and  that is about it I think it's not really  much else out there that you can really  use some outdated sets and some sets in  which you have to create your own rock  faces but that takes a lot of time and  work and generally it's h